00:08:24,270 --> 00:08:25,271
Kelle: OKAY.

232
00:08:25,271 --> 00:08:26,373
Tyra: HAVE A SEAT.

233
00:08:26,373 --> 00:08:27,474
DO YOU HAVE ANY QUESTIONS
OR ANYTHING?

234
00:08:27,474 --> 00:08:28,742
Kelle: YEAH,
I WANNA KNOW

235
00:08:28,742 --> 00:08:30,377
WHAT SOME OF MY STRENGTHS
AND MY WEAKNESSES ARE.

236
00:08:30,377 --> 00:08:32,278
Tyra: WELL, I THINK
YOUR STRENGTH IS YOUR SKIN,

237
00:08:32,278 --> 00:08:34,714
AND THEN THE WEAKNESS IS
YOU DON'T UNDERSTAND YOUR FACE,

238
00:08:34,714 --> 00:08:36,216
'CAUSE YOU ARE
PHOTOGENIC,

239
00:08:36,216 --> 00:08:38,585
BUT THE WAY YOU PLACE YOUR FACE
IN A PICTURE

240
00:08:38,585 --> 00:08:40,486
MAKES YOU
NOT PHOTOGENIC.

241
00:08:40,486 --> 00:08:42,022
Kelle: OKAY, BUT, TYRA,
YOU KNOW WHAT?

242
00:08:42,022 --> 00:08:43,256
IT'S SO DIFFERENT
IN THE MIRROR.

243
00:08:43,256 --> 00:08:45,592
Tyra: NO, KELLE, IT'S NOT
DIFFERENT IN THE MIRROR.

244
00:08:45,592 --> 00:08:47,160
MNH-MNH, THAT MIRROR'S THE
PHOTO-- IT IS THE PHOTO.

245
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:48,395
Kelle: I'M TRYING NOW.

246
00:08:48,395 --> 00:08:49,396
Tyra: GET THAT FIERCE
ON THAT PICTURE.

247
00:08:49,396 --> 00:08:50,764
Kelle: I AM. I AM.

248
00:08:50,764 --> 00:08:51,631
Tyra: SO WHAT DID YOU
THINK MODELING WAS

249
00:08:51,631 --> 00:08:52,699
BEFORE YOU GOT HERE?

250
00:08:52,699 --> 00:08:54,300
Ann: I KNEW
IT WAS HARD.

251
00:08:54,300 --> 00:08:57,037
I JUST--I GUESS I ASSUMED--
BECAUSE I'D ALWAYS BEEN TOLD,

252
00:08:57,037 --> 00:08:58,705
"OH, YOU SHOULD BE A MODEL,
YOU SHOULD BE A MODEL."--

253
00:08:58,705 --> 00:09:00,106
THAT IT WOULD
NATURALLY COME TO ME.

254
00:09:00,106 --> 00:09:01,741
Tyra: DO YOU KNOW WHY YOU'RE
GOOD AT EVERYTHING ELSE?

255
00:09:01,741 --> 00:09:03,243
Ann: WHY?

256
00:09:03,243 --> 00:09:05,545
Tyra: BECAUSE YOU STUDY IT
AND YOU PRACTICE IT.

257
00:09:05,545 --> 00:09:07,213
YOU DIDN'T JUST START
DOING WATER POLO AND SAY,

258
00:09:07,213 --> 00:09:08,481
"OH, A POOL.
THAT'S CUTE.

259
00:09:08,481 --> 00:09:10,283
LET ME GET IN IT WITH MY BIKINI,
AND I'M GONNA WIN."

260
00:09:10,283 --> 00:09:13,086
YOU WALKED INTO THIS MODELING
WORLD AND DIDN'T HAVE A CLUE.

261
00:09:13,086 --> 00:09:14,487
Ann: RIGHT.

262
00:09:14,487 --> 00:09:15,622
Tyra: SO WHAT'S UP, CASSIE?
HOW YOU DOIN'?

263
00:09:15,622 --> 00:09:18,258
Cassie: I'M GLAD I'M HERE,
'CAUSE I DIDN'T COME HERE

264
00:09:18,258 --> 00:09:19,759
SO I COULD GET AWAY
FROM WHAT I DID.

265
00:09:19,759 --> 00:09:21,694
I'M NOT GOING BACK
TO STRIPPING.

266
00:09:21,694 --> 00:09:23,396
Tyra: IF I HAVE ANYTHING
TO DO WITH IT,

267
00:09:23,396 --> 00:09:24,697
YOU AIN'T GOIN' BACK.

268
00:09:24,697 --> 00:09:26,332
I'LL BE COMIN' UP
ON THE STAGE

269
00:09:26,332 --> 00:09:29,035
AND GRABBIN' YOUR LITTLE NAKED
BUTT OFF THAT STAGE AND SAYIN',

270
00:09:29,035 --> 00:09:30,437
"YOU'RE COMIN' HOME
WITH ME, CASSIE.

271
00:09:30,437 --> 00:09:31,971
"WE'RE NOT DOIN'
THIS ANYMORE."

272
00:09:31,971 --> 00:09:33,273
Cassie: THANK YOU,
TYRA.

273
00:09:33,273 --> 00:09:34,707
YOU'RE GONNA MAKE ME CRY
JUST BECAUSE YOU CARE SO MUCH.

274
00:09:34,707 --> 00:09:38,611
Tyra: I DON'T NECESSARILY FEEL
LIKE YOU WANNA BE AT THE TOP

275
00:09:38,611 --> 00:09:40,180
OR EVEN REALLY WANNA
BE HERE.

276
00:09:40,180 --> 00:09:41,614
Jennipher: SEE, AND I DON'T KNOW
WHY PEOPLE THINK THAT.

277
00:09:41,614 --> 00:09:43,383
MAYBE BECAUSE IT DOESN'T
COME ACROSS STRONG

278
00:09:43,383 --> 00:09:45,251
AND I'VE ALWAYS KEPT THAT
TO MYSELF.

279
00:09:45,251 --> 00:09:46,686
Tyra: IN ORDER
TO WIN THIS COMPETITION,

280
00:09:46,686 --> 00:09:48,521
OR EVEN TO PROGRESS
FROM WEEK TO WEEK,

281
00:09:48,521 --> 00:09:51,524
THERE'S A FIRE
THAT PEOPLE NEED TO FEEL,

282
00:09:51,524 --> 00:09:53,526
AND I THINK THAT WOULD BE
MY NOTE FOR YOU--

283
00:09:53,526 --> 00:09:55,328
TO LEARN HOW TO WEAR
YOUR EMOTIONS

284
00:09:55,328 --> 00:09:56,396
A LITTLE BIT MORE
ON YOUR SLEEVE

285
00:09:56,396 --> 00:09:57,764
BECAUSE
IT'S ENDEARING.

286
00:09:57,764 --> 00:09:59,432
Jennipher: BASICALLY, TO ME,
WHAT SHE WAS SAYING IS,

287
00:09:59,432 --> 00:10:01,401
IF YOUR PERSONALITY
DOESN'T COME OUT,

288
00:10:01,401 --> 00:10:03,369
I WAS GOING HOME,
IS WHAT I TOOK IT.

289
00:10:03,369 --> 00:10:05,138
Toccara: SOME PEOPLE ASK ME,
"WHAT IS YOUR GOAL?"

290
00:10:05,138 --> 00:10:06,739
AND IT'S LIKE,
I'M HERE TO WIN

291
00:10:06,739 --> 00:10:08,475
AND I'M ALSO HERE
TO BREAK BARRIERS.

292
00:10:08,475 --> 00:10:11,177
I'M HERE TO BE THE FIRST
BLACK PLUS-SIZE SUPERMODEL,

293
00:10:11,177 --> 00:10:13,646
SO SOME PEOPLE ARE LIKE,
"OH, NO, YOU'RE TOO BIG,"

294
00:10:13,646 --> 00:10:15,482
AND EVERYBODY WAS JUST
TELLIN' ME STUFF, YOU KNOW?

295
00:10:15,482 --> 00:10:16,616
Tyra: HOW DOES IT FEEL

296
00:10:16,616 --> 00:10:18,585
WHEN THOSE NEGATIVE ONES
ARE SAYING THAT TO YOU?

297
00:10:18,585 --> 00:10:21,187
Toccara: I'VE BEEN THROUGH SO
MUCH NEGATIVE STUFF IN MY LIFE.

298
00:10:21,187 --> 00:10:22,455
I MEAN,
MY MOM DIDN'T RAISE ME,

299
00:10:22,455 --> 00:10:24,290
AND MY DADDY
DIDN'T RAISE ME,

300
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:26,326
AND, UM...

301
00:10:26,326 --> 00:10:27,560
WHY ARE YOU
MAKING ME CRY, TYRA?

302
00:10:27,560 --> 00:10:28,595
Tyra: OKAY,

303
00:10:28,595 --> 00:10:30,096
THIS IS A BEAUTIFUL PART
OF YOU,

304
00:10:30,096 --> 00:10:31,631
AND THIS IS-- THIS IS GONNA
MAKE YOU A BETTER PERSON

305
00:10:31,631 --> 00:10:33,266
BY BEING A HUMAN BEING

306
00:10:33,266 --> 00:10:34,634
AND NOT JUST BEING
ONE-DIMENSIONAL.

307
00:10:34,634 --> 00:10:35,635
Toccara: YEAH.

308
00:10:35,635 --> 00:10:37,103
Tyra: IT'S TRUE.

309
00:10:37,103 --> 00:10:38,438
Toccara: THAT'S WHY
I FIGURE,

310
00:10:38,438 --> 00:10:40,273
MAYBE ONCE I GET
TO WHERE I WANNA GO,

311
00:10:40,273 --> 00:10:42,275
MAYBE I CAN HAVE MY MOMMY,
I CAN HAVE MY DADDY,

312
00:10:42,275 --> 00:10:46,079
AND THEN I JUST REALIZE THAT
I DON'T HAVE POWER.

313
00:10:46,079 --> 00:10:47,447
LIKE, SHE HAS
TO WANT IT.

314
00:10:47,447 --> 00:10:49,115
MY DADDY
HAS TO WANT IT.

315
00:10:49,115 --> 00:10:52,118
SO IT DOESN'T MATTER
WHO I AM OR WHO I'LL BECOME.

316
00:10:52,118 --> 00:10:53,253
THEY JUST HAVE TO WANT--

317
00:10:53,253 --> 00:10:54,454
I CAN'T MAKE THEM
DO ANYTHING.

318
00:10:54,454 --> 00:10:55,622
Tyra: BUT DO YOU
THINK MAYBE

319
00:10:55,622 --> 00:10:57,257
BY YOU BEING
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL

320
00:10:57,257 --> 00:10:59,626
OR JUST BEING SUCCESSFUL
IN ANY TYPE OF WAY HERE

321
00:10:59,626 --> 00:11:02,295
WILL INSPIRE THEM
TO WANT IT?

322
00:11:02,295 --> 00:11:03,663
YOU KNOW,
"LOOK WHAT SHE DID"?

323
00:11:03,663 --> 00:11:05,331
Toccara: I CAN'T CRY
NO MORE.

324
00:11:05,331 --> 00:11:08,101
I DON'T WANNA
CRY NO MORE.

325
00:11:08,101 --> 00:11:12,539
I CAN'T GO RIGHT BACK
TO THE SAME THING--

326
00:11:12,539 --> 00:11:14,107
THE SAME THING.

327
00:11:14,107 --> 00:11:15,542
IT'S LIKE...

328
00:11:15,542 --> 00:11:16,576
Tyra: BUT DO YOU KNOW
WHEN YOU'RE CRYIN'

329
00:11:16,576 --> 00:11:17,977
THAT MEANS
IT'S STILL THERE,

330
00:11:17,977 --> 00:11:19,112
AND IT'S STILL INSIDE?

331
00:11:19,112 --> 00:11:20,713
Toccara: YOU KNOW,

332
00:11:20,713 --> 00:11:22,415
WHY CRY ABOUT SOMETHING THAT
YOU CAN'T DO ANYTHING ABOUT,

333
00:11:22,415 --> 00:11:23,683
YOU KNOW?

334
00:11:23,683 --> 00:11:26,085
I--AND MAYBE I'VE TOUGHENED
MYSELF UP, YOU KNOW?

335
00:11:26,085 --> 00:11:28,221
BECAUSE I-I CAN'T
DO ANYTHING ABOUT IT.

336
00:11:28,221 --> 00:11:30,256
I CAN'T DWELL
ON IT.

337
00:11:30,256 --> 00:11:32,192
I CAN'T BE
STUCK ON IT.

338
00:11:32,192 --> 00:11:34,160
I CAN'T LET IT
AFFECT ME.

339
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:36,129
I CAN'T--
YOU KNOW, I CAN'T.

340
00:11:36,129 --> 00:11:37,664
I JUST GOTTA LET IT GO.

341
00:11:37,664 --> 00:11:39,265
I CAN'T KEEP--

342
00:11:39,265 --> 00:11:40,300
Tyra: NOW LOOK WHERE YOU ARE
RIGHT NOW.

343
00:11:40,300 --> 00:11:41,668
YOU ARE HERE,

344
00:11:41,668 --> 00:11:43,169
AND YOUR SISTER,
11 YEARS OLD,

345
00:11:43,169 --> 00:11:44,704
IS RIGHT THERE
LOOKIN' AT YOU,

346
00:11:44,704 --> 00:11:47,640
AND I THINK YOU HAVE
TO USE THAT AS POWER.

347
00:11:47,640 --> 00:11:49,609
THAT'S WHAT'S
FUELING YOU.

348
00:11:49,609 --> 00:11:51,244
THAT'S WHAT GIVES YOU
THAT BEAUTIFUL SMILE

349
00:11:51,244 --> 00:11:52,745
AND THAT
BEAUTIFUL ENERGY

350
00:11:52,745 --> 00:11:54,280
AND THAT'S WHAT'S
MAKING THOSE PICTURES BEAUTIFUL.

351
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:56,549
IT'S WHERE
YOU COME FROM.

352
00:11:56,549 --> 00:11:58,251
COME HERE
AND SIT WITH ME.

353
00:11:58,251 --> 00:12:00,320
Toccara: I CAN'T
CHANGE THEM, TYRA.

354
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:01,588
Tyra: NO,
YOU CAN'T CHANGE THEM,

355
00:12:01,588 --> 00:12:03,122
BUT YOU CAN DO
FOR YOU,

356
00:12:03,122 --> 00:12:04,524
AND YOU CAN DO
FOR YOUR SISTER,

357
00:12:04,524 --> 00:12:07,327
AND YOU CAN BE AN INSPIRATION
FOR YOUR MOTHER.

358
00:12:07,327 --> 00:12:09,028
SHE'S GONNA SEE
HER BABY

359
00:12:09,028 --> 00:12:12,699
AND BE LIKE, "OH, MY GOD.
I SCREWED UP SO BAD.

360
00:12:12,699 --> 00:12:14,234
"I DON'T KNOW HOW
MY BABY GOT THERE,

361
00:12:14,234 --> 00:12:15,535
"BUT SHE GOT THERE."

362
00:12:15,535 --> 00:12:17,070
Toccara:
(sobbing)

363
00:12:17,070 --> 00:12:19,405
Tyra:
SHE GOT THERE.

364
00:12:25,077 --> 00:12:26,178
Toccara: I DON'T
BELIEVE IT.

365
00:12:26,178 --> 00:12:27,746
SHE MADE ME CRY.

366
00:12:27,746 --> 00:12:30,449
WE WAS JUST TALKING ABOUT
MY FAMILY AND ME GROWING UP.

367
00:12:30,449 --> 00:12:33,485
AND I WAS JUST...
(sighs)

368
00:12:33,485 --> 00:12:35,120
I'M STILL SHOCKED AT MYSELF
THAT I CRIED.

369
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:38,023
I COULDN'T BELIEVE THAT I HAD
TEARS COMING OUT OF MY EYES.

370
00:12:38,023 --> 00:12:39,558
BECAUSE, LIKE I SAID,
THIS IS JUST MY LIFE.

371
00:12:39,558 --> 00:12:41,427
THIS IS JUST WHAT
I HAD TO GO THROUGH.

372
00:12:41,427 --> 00:12:42,661
I HAD TO BE
SUPPORTIVE.

373
00:12:42,661 --> 00:12:43,896
I HAD
TO BE STRONG.

374
00:12:43,896 --> 00:12:45,964
SO I HAD TO BE THAT ONE
THAT PEOPLE COULD COME TO

375
00:12:45,964 --> 00:12:47,533
AND CRY ON,
YOU KNOW?

376
00:12:47,533 --> 00:12:49,168
I WANNA BE AN INSPIRATION
TO PEOPLE, YOU KNOW,

377
00:12:49,168 --> 00:12:52,838
BUT THE ULTIMATE GOAL HERE
IS TO BE THE LAST ONE STANDING.

378
00:12:52,838 --> 00:12:54,940
SO YOU GOTTA SURVIVE.

379
00:12:59,445 --> 00:13:00,979
Kelle: (sobs)

380
00:13:00,979 --> 00:13:03,015
THE PAST THREE PANELS,

381
00:13:03,015 --> 00:13:05,818
I'VE HAD PROBABLY
THE WORST PHOTOS IN THE GROUP.

382
00:13:05,818 --> 00:13:07,720
I'VE HAD
A PENIS.

383
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:10,656
I'VE BEEN A DEER IN HEADLIGHTS
IN THE MIDDLE OF A CEMETERY.

384
00:13:10,656 --> 00:13:13,859
I'VE BEEN A PLATYPUS
THAT JUST CAME FROM A DENTIST.

385
00:13:13,859 --> 00:13:15,060
THE MIRROR
IS THE CAMERA.

386
00:13:15,060 --> 00:13:16,528
I WAS JUST SEEING MYSELF,

387
00:13:16,528 --> 00:13:20,699
AND I'M LIKE,
"OH, MY GOD, I'M HIDEOUS."

388
00:13:20,699 --> 00:13:21,767
(sobs)

389
00:13:21,767 --> 00:13:23,435
Toccara: WHERE'S KELLE?

390
00:13:23,435 --> 00:13:25,104
DON'T BE CRYING.

391
00:13:25,104 --> 00:13:26,438
COME HERE,
MAMA.

392
00:13:26,438 --> 00:13:27,806
WHAT'S WRONG?

393
00:13:27,806 --> 00:13:29,608
Kelle: I CAN'T LOOK AT MYSELF
IN THE MIRROR.

394
00:13:29,608 --> 00:13:30,843
Toccara: (laughs)

395
00:13:30,843 --> 00:13:32,444
Kelle: I'M SO SERIOUS,
YOU DON'T UNDERSTAND.

396
00:13:32,444 --> 00:13:33,579
I JUST SPENT
THE LAST HOUR--

397
00:13:33,579 --> 00:13:35,414
EVERYTIME I LOOK IN THE MIRROR,
I'M CRYING.

398
00:13:35,414 --> 00:13:36,782
Toccara: BEFORE YOU WAS ALL
IN THE MIRROR.

399
00:13:36,782 --> 00:13:38,417
YOU COULDN'T GET YOUR ASS
OUT THE MIRROR.

400
00:13:38,417 --> 00:13:39,852
EVERY TIME I TURNED AROUND
YOU WAS IN THE MIRROR.

401
00:13:39,852 --> 00:13:41,987
YOU WAS HERE, YOU WAS HERE,
YOU WAS THERE.

402
00:13:41,987 --> 00:13:43,689
KELLE CAME
IN THIS COMPETITION,

403
00:13:43,689 --> 00:13:45,424
AND SHE WAS JUST LIKE,

404
00:13:45,424 --> 00:13:46,759
"OH, I'M BEAUTIFUL."

405
00:13:46,759 --> 00:13:49,561
AND THE JUDGES HAVE TOTALLY
BROKE HER.

406
00:13:49,561 --> 00:13:50,796
IT'S NOT
GOOD PRACTICE.

407
00:13:50,796 --> 00:13:51,730
THIS IS
NOT HEALTHY.

408
00:13:51,730 --> 00:13:52,931
Kelle: I CAN'T.

409
00:13:52,931 --> 00:13:54,166
Toccara: COME
TO MY ROOM,

410
00:13:54,166 --> 00:13:55,434
SIT ON MY BED
AND TALK TO ME.

411
00:13:55,434 --> 00:13:56,735
GET OUT OF HERE,
COME ON, LET'S GO.

412
00:13:56,735 --> 00:13:58,771
I SAID,
"GIRL, GET OUT THAT MIRROR.

413
00:13:58,771 --> 00:14:00,606
"COME TO
MY ROOM."

414
00:14:00,606 --> 00:14:02,040
Kelle: I REALIZED
WHAT IT WAS.

415
00:14:02,040 --> 00:14:04,643
IT'S THIS PART OF MY MOUTH--
RIGHT HERE.

416
00:14:04,643 --> 00:14:06,979
IT'S LIKE AN EXTRA LAYER
OF FAT OR SOMETHING.

417
00:14:06,979 --> 00:14:09,014
SO IT'S LIKE
A SNOUT.

418
00:14:09,014 --> 00:14:10,649
AND THAT'S WHY I HAVE--
LIKE, YOU SEE IT? LOOK.

419
00:14:10,649 --> 00:14:13,018
LIKE, SHE HAS THAT,
TOO.

420
00:14:13,018 --> 00:14:14,586
SEE, LOOK.

421
00:14:14,586 --> 00:14:15,687
LOOK AT IT.

422
00:14:15,687 --> 00:14:17,089
YOU SEE HOW IT'S LIKE
A SNOUT PART?

423
00:14:17,089 --> 00:14:19,057
Toccara: OKAY,
BUT WHAT'S UGLY ABOUT THAT?

424
00:14:19,057 --> 00:14:21,493
Kelle: I'M JUST SAYING
I DON'T-- I DIDN'T--

425
00:14:21,493 --> 00:14:24,096
I WAS IN DENIAL
ABOUT MY SNOUT,

426
00:14:24,096 --> 00:14:25,631
AND NOW I KNOW.

427
00:14:25,631 --> 00:14:26,965
AND SO IT'S JUST HARD
TO WORK.

428
00:14:26,965 --> 00:14:28,400
YOU'RE VERY LIMITED--

429
00:14:28,400 --> 00:14:29,501
Toccara: WELL, OBVIOUSLY
SHE'S DOING SOMETHING,

430
00:14:29,501 --> 00:14:30,669
'CAUSE BITCH
IS GETTING PAID.

431
00:14:30,669 --> 00:14:31,804
Kelle: 'CAUSE SHE KNOWS--

432
00:14:31,804 --> 00:14:33,939
Toccara: SO OBVIOUSLY
BITCH WORKIN' IT.

433
00:14:33,939 --> 00:14:36,909
Kelle: SO THAT'S WHAT
I LOOK LIKE IN THE MAGAZINE.

434
00:14:36,909 --> 00:14:38,677
Toccara: I'M GONNA KICK YOU
OUT OF MY ROOM IN A MINUTE.

435
00:14:44,583 --> 00:14:47,886
Toccara: YES!
TYRA MAIL!

436
00:14:47,886 --> 00:14:49,588
"DO YOU EVER
HAVE A DREAM

437
00:14:49,588 --> 00:14:51,990
THAT YOU WERE WALKING AROUND
IN ONLY YOUR UNDERWEAR?"

438
00:14:51,990 --> 00:14:53,792
Nicole: WE GET
OUR TYRA MAIL,

439
00:14:53,792 --> 00:14:57,496
AND I'M THINKING WE HAVE TO DO
A RUNWAY SHOW IN PANTIES.

440
00:14:57,496 --> 00:14:59,164
Eva: YOU THINK WE NEED
TO WEAR SEXY PANTIES?

441
00:14:59,164 --> 00:15:00,632
Yaya: NO,
THEY'LL GIVE US UNDIES.

442
00:15:00,632 --> 00:15:02,467
Eva: I'M GONNA BE ME.

443
00:15:02,467 --> 00:15:04,670
GONNA BE WEARING
MY LUCKY LADY DRAWERS.

444
00:15:09,741 --> 00:15:13,512
Amanda: EVERYBODY KNOWS
LA PERLA IS "IT" IN LINGERIE.

445
00:15:13,512 --> 00:15:15,480
IT IS JUST MWAH,
BEAUTIFUL.

446
00:15:15,480 --> 00:15:16,481
Simon: HI THERE.

447
00:15:16,481 --> 00:15:17,716
HI.

448
00:15:17,716 --> 00:15:21,053
OKAY, GIRLS,
WELCOME TO LA PERLA.

449
00:15:21,053 --> 00:15:23,522
MY NAME
IS SIMON DOONAN.

450
00:15:23,522 --> 00:15:25,591
I'M THE CREATIVE DIRECTOR
OF BARNEYS.

451
00:15:25,591 --> 00:15:28,727
I UNDERSTAND YESTERDAY
YOU LEARNED A LOT ABOUT POSING.

452
00:15:28,727 --> 00:15:31,029
AND TODAY'S CHALLENGE
IS ALL ABOUT POSING.

453
00:15:31,029 --> 00:15:36,602
